### 2. Example AI-Powered Writing Workflow
@2-workflow

- The split: the human thinks and validates, the AI does the structured steps.
- (AI) The steps below are the ones I use for every long-form piece.

#### Step 1. Brain-dumping
- A folder and `braindump.mkd`; dictate or type ideas in any language.
- Light Markdown structure; `<TBD>` tags mark the gaps.

#### Step 2. Creating an Outline
- The agent builds `outline.mkd` from the braindump; I refine it by hand.
- `@` lines set section file names and their order.

#### Step 3. Generating section files
- Section files are generated from the outline with the rules files.
- Several short files instead of one long draft: better focus and targeted edits.

#### Step 4. Expanding and Validating
- I expand the AI sections where micro-ideas are missing, by hand or with the agent.
- (AI) Save the short version before a big edit, to be able to go back.

### Final steps
@3-final-steps

- A script combines the section files into one Markdown file.
- "Paste from Markdown" into Google Docs, then images and final formatting by hand.

### Conclusion
@4-conclusion

- The IDE takes over the technical steps and leaves the creative ones to the author.
